Subject: [PATCH] drivers: can: mcan: Zero out frame struct when constructing
 new CAN frame

Backport of upstream commit 1e1855620db4350bc8c686094e591a9d2bcb348b.

Currently, the CAN frame is only zeroed at the start of the function,
and if multiple frames are read in a single pass, any flags that were
ORed into the flags field will be carried into later frames, even if the
later frame should not actually have those flags set. Instead, leave the
frame variable uninitialised and zero it out on each iteration loop.

Signed-off-by: Zee Yudenko <zyudenko@internships.antmicro.com>

diff --git a/drivers/can/can_mcan.c b/drivers/can/can_mcan.c
--- a/drivers/can/can_mcan.c
+++ b/drivers/can/can_mcan.c
@@ -719,7 +719,7 @@ static void can_mcan_get_message(const struct device *dev, uint16_t fifo_offset,
 	const struct can_mcan_config *config = dev->config;
 	const struct can_mcan_callbacks *cbs = config->callbacks;
 	struct can_mcan_rx_fifo_hdr hdr;
-	struct can_frame frame = {0};
+	struct can_frame frame;
 	can_rx_callback_t cb;
 	void *user_data;
 	uint32_t get_idx;
@@ -745,6 +745,8 @@ static void can_mcan_get_message(const struct device *dev, uint16_t fifo_offset,
 			return;
 		}
 
+		memset(&frame, 0, sizeof(frame));
+
 		frame.dlc = hdr.dlc;
 
 		if (hdr.rtr != 0) {
